'''Scientists''' were researchers in the fields of biology, chemistry and physics. During the [[High Republic Era]], the [[Galactic Society of Creature Enthusiasts]] was founded by a group of like-[[Brain|minded]] scientists and adventurers that were interested in researching and cataloging the myriad of new species that were discovered on the [[Galactic Republic|Republic]]'s [[Galactic Frontier|frontier worlds]].<ref name="Activity Sheet" /> The [[Kaminoan]]s were scientists who specialized in [[cloning]] technology. [[Galen Walton Erso]] was a scientist and polymath employed by the [[Galactic Empire]] to be a crucial part in the development of the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]].<ref name="Catalyst">''[[Catalyst: A Rogue One Novel]]''</ref> [[Zare Leonis]]'s parents, [[Leo Leonis|Leo]] and [[Tepha Leonis]], were agricultural scientists employed by the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Ministry of Agriculture]].<ref name="Edge">''[[Servants of the Empire: Edge of the Galaxy]]''</ref> [[Galactic Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious]] enlisted the scientist [[Cylo]] to look into possible replacements for his [[Sith apprentice|apprentice]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]].<ref name="Darth Vader 5">[[Darth Vader (2015) 5|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 5]]</ref> The [[Gender|female]] [[Tulon Voidgazer]] was a scientist who served aboard the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[superweapon]] before its [[Battle of Yavin|destruction]].<ref name="Darth Vader 6">[[Darth Vader (2015) 6|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 6]]</ref>

{{Science-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
On [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars The Complete Season Two|''The Clone Wars'' season two]] featurette ''Attack of the Zillo Beast'', concept artist [[Kilian Plunkett]] poked fun at how many "well meaning" scientists like [[Doctor]] [[Sionver Boll]] aren't interested in solving societal issues, but as they mean well their mistakes are entirely forgivable.

